Loom: a concat whose result lives in explicit physical registers (AIE2P) is reserved from its earliest unit's start
with per-unit start points, as fragmented tied-source assemblies already are: a whole register cannot be split, so a
piece placed before the reservation forces copies of the others. GPU sets byte-identical; changes 15 of the NPU
split's 27 images (NPU gate: pp2048 split window 00 bit-identical,
hidden / logits / all_logits md5 equal).
diff --git a/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/concat_reservation.c b/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/concat_reservation.c
index d204683816..f7377199de 100644
--- a/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/concat_reservation.c
